It is convenient for those users that do not want to use UWUW to be able to interact with FluDAG in a more simplistic way. Therefore we should reintroduce the first method we used to define materials tags for FluDAG. Namely by adding volumes to groups of the form mat:NAME where NAME is an 8 character long string, which immediately produces the appropriate ASSIGNMAt card. This can be done in a similar way to how we interact with the legacy MCNP workflow, something like

```
UWUWU *uwuw = new UWUW("filenaname");
if ( uwuw->material_library().length() == 0 ) { 
   simple_workflow();
else
  uwuw_workflow();
```

Such that if UWUW materials are found, then we use the UWUW workflow, otherwise assume its the simple one.

Using the pyne::particle class as a source of valid particle names, it would be straightforward to allow MCNP5 and MCNP6 to use a common function to produce importance tags in the UWUW workflow. This can be done by something like either

```
if MCNP5 {
  allowed_particles = {"neutron","photon","electron"}
else if MCNP6 {
  all the particles 
} else {
  fail
}
```

Checks should be put in uwuw_preprocessor.cpp to make sure the importance tags are valid and that every volume has an importance assigned.

